A||N||18||Devotshka||Need ideas for third brake light||||5||
Z||000000||Devotshka||08-25-2001||06:42 PM||||Hey peoples.  My roadster is almost to the stage of building a new third brake light, but i am stumped as to what would look least obtrusive.  <BR>I have two 24-LED brake lights (without enclosures) that i have to play with aside from traditional 1980's style brake lights, and after much consideration, have decided NOT to gut my wing to fit one in there, so i seem to be limited to a light mounted on decklid or firewall, or (Gaaa!) a pedestal mount... Does anyone have any ingenious ways to mount a brakelight on a topless car floating around in there head?<BR>Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Songman||08-25-2001||07:08 PM||||Would be nice if you could somehow come up with a way to remove your trunk lock and use an old Pontiac arrowhead right in the middle of the trunk and somehow light it. I have seen cars do that. Maybe a Cadillac Allante... Would be very cool though!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||7
Z||000002||Devotshka||08-25-2001||07:59 PM||||i thought about working a light into the crease of the decklid right above the keylock, but theres just not enough room to get it in there and be aesthetically pleasing (imho) when the decklid is opened.  <BR>I've been toying around with the idea of integrating the light into my rollbar.... thats a helluva lot of work tho and i gotta get it right the first time  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||9
Z||000003||starfighter007@msn.com||08-25-2001||09:29 PM||||If you have the talent to do it my vote is in the wing ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Devotshka||08-26-2001||01:59 PM||||Well, i probably *could* do it in the wing, but i really don't want to brake into a wing that is mint. If i had a spare to do it to so that i could switch back, it'd probably be a different story.  <P>I thought it might be neat to put one of those really long LED strips into the roofline along the windshield, until i realised my face would turn red when i hit the brakes :P<P>Oh well.... -someone- must have some ideas....||||reg||4
Z||000005||StuGood||08-26-2001||04:46 PM||||How about on the back of a headband, you have to put on when you drive (and one for your passenger, too   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">?<P>"Here, put this on."<P>"Huh?  What's with the wire?  What is this - a car with an electric chair?  Or a lie detector - you don't trust me, do you?"<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>Okay, enough of that.  If you are using a stock Fiero hood, could you fair it into the "hump" in the middle (between the two decklid grills)?  Just a thought...<p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 08-26-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000006||Devotshka||08-26-2001||04:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by StuGood:<BR><B> could you fair it into the "hump" in the middle (between the two decklid grills)?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hmmm.... possible... i'll have to eyeball it;  i think it would need to be raised a bit at the rear of the hump to change from that downward slope to a vertical/near vertical position towards the end for the LEDs, not sure how much visibility there would be past the wing.   Definately a possibility, thanks!<BR>Any other ideas people?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||gargoyle||08-26-2001||04:58 PM||||I vote for NO third brake light. I don't think you have to have it if your other lights work. Besides everybody got one, be different. If you are worried about being seen change your bulbs over to led. They are much brighter or wire in a modulator from a motorcycle so they flash when you brake. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Devotshka||08-26-2001||05:06 PM||||Yeah, thats about where i was when i decided to ask you guys.... no 3rd light.  But like i said, i have two LONG led strips to play with so far... still exploring options, and i figure if its about being different, thats why my car has been naked for the past 2 months getting the faceift  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Its to the point now where i can actually *see* the progress and so the desire to do more is overabundant.... Overall though, i still just wanna go drive my car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by gargoyle:<BR><B>I vote for NO third brake light. I don't think you have to have it if your other lights work. Besides everybody got one, be different. If you are worried about being seen change your bulbs over to led. They are much brighter or wire in a modulator from a motorcycle so they flash when you brake. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||mrgone||08-26-2001||08:08 PM||||why not hook the lighted pontiac to the brake lights<P>or how about the lower bumper.. <BR>glass it into the roof at the back, above where the stock one goes||||reg||1
Z||000010||HummelHund||08-26-2001||09:03 PM||||Just taking a look at the 88' Merkur XR4Ti sitting in my driveway, what about finding a wing that already has a third brake light in it? The XR does, and I've always thought it'd look good on a Fiero, but for some reason my dad just won't let me rip it off his car to put on my 84' SE. He's funny like that.<BR>I can't think of any other cars with the light in the spoiler off the top of my head, but I'm sure there are others out there.<P><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6, The "Buzz Bomb". (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>84' SE 2M4 WS6 (Dad's Project)||||reg||1
Z||000011||Max The Chainsaw||08-26-2001||11:12 PM||||Mount one to the back of each seat's headrest, you did say it was a convertable didn't you?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Devotshka||08-26-2001||11:57 PM||||Yep, roadster.... headrests won't work because of the rollbar (and theres no way i'm cutting into my leather  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">).<P>Right now i'm thinking of the molding it into the decklid hump idea, or possibly building up a unit on the firewall, just below the rollbar.<P>I can't do the 'PONTIAC' idea because its not a fastback, and the notchback alternative of using the embossing on bumper is out, as i smoothed that over several years ago.  I'm sticking with the stock wing (haven't seen any others that I like on fieros yet), so a wing brake light is out too;  no plans on gutting my wing at the moment.<P>Thanks guys, keep em coming  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000013||Ryan Wright||08-27-2001||12:13 AM||||How about down low - just underneath the rear bumper? Those LED lights are bright; I doubt anybody would miss it down there. Might look neat.<P>The decklid idea between the vents is a good one, too.<BR><P>------------------<BR>-Ryan Wright (http://www.ryanwright.com)||||reg||1
Z||000014||GOLDSE||08-27-2001||01:51 PM||||Early 90's Corvette convertibles came with a third brake light mounted on the rear deck.  Was a little hump of a brake light.  I was going to integrate this into my Chevy truck at the time, before trucks had third brake lights.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||LZeitgeist||08-27-2001||01:56 PM||||When I had my dreams of a Fiero convertible, I had planned on getting the third brake light assembly from a late '80s Ford Taurus station wagon and integrating it into the rear of the decklid hump, something along the lines of what the Testarossa uses. (If my memory serves - this was a long time ago.)<P>Please don't use one of those stupid little E.T.-looking third brakelights from a Porsche, though - I wanna knock those stupid little things off the cars with a baseball bat when I see them. &lt;bleah&gt; ::chuckle::<P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001||||reg||1
Z||000016||ChopTop||08-27-2001||02:14 PM||||I believe the brake light should be mounted up high.  When President Regan first requested automotive manufacturers to install 3rd brake lights it was out of safety concerns (read heads that barely topped the steering wheel).  Now, when it seems half our driving population drive high riding SUVs the idea makes more sense than ever.  Incorporating it into your rollbar is a good idea.  ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Steve Normington||08-27-2001||02:15 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by gargoyle:<BR><B>I vote for NO third brake light. I don't think you have to have it if your other lights work. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I'd worry that if someone hit you, they could claim it was because you didn't have the third brake light.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000018||Devotshka||08-27-2001||08:21 PM||||I agree on the porshe pedestal mount...they make me want to puke (hence earlier comment).  I am going to have to find some old taurus pictures, i can't quite remember how they looked on there, but i do *need* the light.  <BR>To the best of my knowledge, as far as the law goes, if something was put there from the factory for safety purposes, its not legal to remove it.... then again i don't have a roof soooooo..............<BR>The problem with putting it into the rollbar is getting a perfect cut the first time, i'm going to have to draw everything out on paper roughly 23 times before i'm certain its going to be right, even then mistakes happen... personally i don't want to have to have another 6 foot anodized bar made for me if i can avoid it.  I still want to field all possibilities, as i'm not dead-set on the rollbar light yet, its jsut an idea at this point, not a plan yet.<BR>Thanks again people.||||reg||1
